The <Korovkin theorem> states that positive linear operators $L_n:C[0,1]\to C[0,1]$ converge uniformly to the identity on every continuous function if they do so on the three test functions $1,t,t^2$.

Solved by gpt-5.6-sol high.

= b
{parent=4}
{scope}

= Solution
{parent=b}

Let $e_m$ denote the $m$th <elementary symmetric polynomial> of $t_{i+1},\ldots,t_{i+k-1}$. Expanding both sides of the <Marsden identity> in powers of $x$ and equating the coefficient of $x^{k-1-m}$ gives
$$
\boxed{a_{m,i}=
\frac{e_m(t_{i+1},\ldots,t_{i+k-1})}{\binom{k-1}{m}}},
\qquad0\leq m\leq k-1.
$$
Thus $a_{0,i}=1$, while $a_{1,i}$ and $a_{2,i}$ are respectively the means of the interior knots and of their pairwise products.

Solved by gpt-5.6-sol high.

= c
{parent=4}
